# REQUIRES: haydn
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/far-call-e96.yaml -o %t.call.o
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/far-target-e96.yaml -o %t.far.o
# Stamp product EF_HAYDN_E96 (e_flags=0x1). yaml2obj has no Haydn e_flags bit
# names; LLD rejects unprofiled zero flags fail-closed (matches BundleSim).
# RUN: %python -c "import struct,sys;f=open(sys.argv[1],'r+b');f.seek(36);f.write(struct.pack('<I',1));f.close()" %t.call.o
# RUN: %python -c "import struct,sys;f=open(sys.argv[1],'r+b');f.seek(36);f.write(struct.pack('<I',1));f.close()" %t.far.o
# RUN: not ld.lld %t.call.o %t.far.o -o %t -T %S/thunk-e96-geometry.ld 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
#
# D1.57 fail-closed restamp (assembler-independent, yaml2obj path): an
# out-of-range R_HAYDN_CallSImm20 must NOT produce a veneer — the retired
# R0-borrowing template was wrong-code. The link fails with the explicit
# veneer-ABI-gap diagnostic (D1.57 / ISA-70); no __haydn_thunk symbol and
# no 3 × EncodedBytes Defined::size = 36 object are created. The base
# (non-WIDE) CallSImm20 kind is pinned here — it is the legacy row the
# shared dispatch historically accepted.

# CHECK: error: {{.*}}.o:({{.*}}relocation R_HAYDN_CallSImm20 to '{{.*}}' needs a linker range-extension veneer{{.*}}Haydn veneer ABI is not approved (D1.57 / ISA-70)
# CHECK-NOT: __haydn_thunk
